e remembered;¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ)And wickedness shall be broken as a tree.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/He evil entreateth the barren that beareth not:¦layout ‚¤textÙ And doeth not good to the widow.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*He draweth also the mighty with his power:¦layout ‚¤textÙ)He riseth up, and no man is sure of life.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ;Though it be given him to be in safety, whereon he resteth;¦layout ‚¤textÙ!Yet his eyes are upon their ways.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ1They are exalted for a little while, but are gone¦layout ‚¤textÙ<And brought low; they are taken out of the way as all other,¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ,And cut off as the tops of the ears of corn.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ1And if it be not so now, who will make me a liar,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And make my speech nothing worth?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse